WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.450
I've been waiting for you.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.910
Are you a Dragoon, just like Zefiris?

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:46.620
Unlike her, I lost most of my 
abilities in the Genesis Wars.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.130
At the moment, I am an emulation 
running on a virtual system

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.460
that I constructed within this 
fortress' central control system.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.590
I have no idea what she just said...

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.530
Perhaps if you thought of it as, 
she transferred her spirit here

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.070
into the Skid when she lost her body.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.060
Right...

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:09.730
It's beyond her current capabilities 
to control all of the Skid's systems,

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:15.670
so we are having her instruct us in 
the ship's operation and supervise us.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.780
We heard all about you from Natalie.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.740
About you, and about what 
this world really is.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.700
What it really is?

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.710
"Battle Hymn of the Two Princesses"

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.940
This signature is strange...

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.570
It's like a Dragoon, but it's...

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.490
Even an ancient relic like that 
could prove to be a minor nuisance

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.570
if it's under the control of a Dragoon.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.700
We'd better destroy it, shouldn't we?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.440
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:09.910
This world is a fabrication that 
was created to control you humans.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.710
Your very existence is the last 
hope left to us by our master.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.840
The final trap meant to smash 
the shell of this world.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.970
Final trap?

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.720
Natalie, don't you think 
it's too early for this?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.680
Why do you say that?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.100
These others were able to comprehend it.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.390
And these three have actually 
faced Peacemakers in combat

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.900
and been in contact with you 
several times, haven't they?

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.400
I think they're capable of understanding it.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.900
I'm not so sure.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.780
I don't think anything you say

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.950
to this carefree princess 
would get through to her.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.880
Who are you calling carefree?!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.030
I haven't exactly had it easy, you know!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.870
My point is that if you don't understand 
what that suffering was <i>for</i>,

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.750
it was all for nothing.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.460
Who do you think you are?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.920
Pacifica Cassul.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.920
There is not much time remaining until 
you will manifest your unique abilities.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.620
I would like you to fully understand 
your purpose while there is time.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.180
What do you mean, my purpose?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.360
What are you talking about?

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.720
What's all this about unique 
abilities and traps?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.310
Who <i>are </i>you people?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.350
Princess Senes.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.730
What is it?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.520
Giat's Second Fleet is approaching, 
deployed in a battle array.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.770
Ship count is 29, and all are armed vessels.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.780
They don't seriously mean 
to attack us, do they?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.070
Could be.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:26.910
Maybe my insane brothers have come 
up with an excuse to get rid of me.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.540
Even so, to openly attack us...

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.000
Eirote, I'll let you handle things here.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.420
For starters, we need to 
find out what it really is.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.280
Stand by for cannon attack.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:41.670
Stand by for cannon attack!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.130
What's our status?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.650
Second Fleet still closing in.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.090
Range, 88 hex.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.430
Assume class two battle preparations.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.060
Roger.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:54.100
Once everyone is in position, disengage 
the seal on the Fomalhaut Flare.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.650
Once it's set to force 3, stand by.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.020
Second Fleet is opening fire!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.740
Are you seriously going to try this, brother?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.600
Providence Breaker Pacifica Cassul.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:19.130
You are the primary key to smashing the 
world that is under Peacemaker control.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:24.050
The reason they are using the Church of 
Mauser in a desperate attempt to stop us

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.470
is because they fear our plan.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.590
Hey, wait a minute...

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.350
You're not telling me the reason she's 
called the poison that will destroy the world

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.310
and we've had people try 
to kill us right and left

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.890
is all because of something 
that you guys set up, are you?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.190
That's not quite...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.560
Exactly.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.480
This plan regarding the Providence 
Breaker, the breaker of divine law,

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.320
and the Guardians, her protectors,

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.360
was set in motion by us and our master.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.290
Guardians? You mean me and Raquel?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.790
You are not the only ones.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:02.210
These other people also 
carry the Guardian gene.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.090
Wait, that's...

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.260
Leo!

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.050
Winia!

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:14.430
Berkens! Elfitine!

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.020
Keydarf...

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.440
Dad... Mom...

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.320
While these people may 
carry the Guardian gene,

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.660
it is not expressed as strongly 
in them as it is in you.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.620
They are the people who carry the genes 
that we scattered across this world

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.910
in order to protect the Providence Breaker 
from the interference of the Peacemakers.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.420
That is what a Guardian is.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.550
Deck 3 has been hit!

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.640
Keep your cool.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.430
Stand by to fire Fomalhaut Flare!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.970
We only need to make it clear

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.980
to my incompetent brother 
exactly what he's up against.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.850
Singe the flank of his flagship.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:02.440
Roger that!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.320
Fire.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:36.850
This means that humans are 
operating a half-dead Dragoon.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.500
In that case, it's simple.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.810
We just need to kill the humans inside.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.780
All ships are maintaining combat speed.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.410
They're closing in in a fan formation!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.240
What? It isn't my brother?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:02.160
Are you saying that you people planned 
from the beginning for Raquel and me

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.270
to be born to play the role 
of Pacifica's protectors?

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:10.300
Is that true, Zefiris?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.130
It means that the genes 
we seeded just happened

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:17.260
to heavily converge within 
you two and were expressed.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.850
And how is that any different?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.640
Shannon...

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.730
So, this was all part of your plan, huh?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.730
Our fighting and our suffering...

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.690
Even the choices we risked our lives for!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.110
C'mon, what's all this mean?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.740
I don't get it.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.780
What do you mean? All part of what plan?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.410
Natalie.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.620
I'm detecting a Peacemaker signature 
aboard one of the approaching ships.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:43.830
It's a Civilian-type,

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.320
but it looks like it's created 
proxies and scattered them.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.530
This way! Hurry!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.150
Raquel...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.070
Did you understand what they 
were talking about back there?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:19.120
I couldn't follow all of the details, 
but it sounded like they were saying

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.950
that our destinies have been 
written out beforehand.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.910
I'm not gonna let anybody 
decide my fate for me!

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.580
What the hell are those monsters?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:31.800
What the heck is this place?

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.920
I can see outside!

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.260
Those aren't windows, though, right?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.890
Eirote, why have you 
brought outsiders onto...

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.430
They have experience with fighting those.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:44.980
Hey, aren't those...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.680
Yeah.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.650
And it looks like there is 
more than one this time.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:53.400
Oh, these are those Peacemaker 
proxies she told us about, huh?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.360
Why aren't you running?!

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.320
Why are you fighting those things?!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.990
You know you can't win!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.490
Stay out of this, civilian.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:04.120
Listen, those things are <i>really </i>powerful.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.690
Last time, lots and lots of villagers 
were killed by just one of those things!

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.460
Don't you dare compare my Scarlet elite 
to your local bumpkin soldiers...

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.490
It's useless.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.420
Recall all your troops and 
seal all your hatches.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.170
That's all you can do.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.300
What good will sealing ourselves 
in do?! Those things will...

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.530
This is just a hypothesis,

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.680
but if we defeat the Peacemaker itself,

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.390
perhaps the proxies would also disappear.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.310
Zefiris and I will go out.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.810
Shannon...

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.090
I'll be fine.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:47.280
My master, fusing with me and 
fighting is not wise at this point.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.530
If I can't use your power at 
a time like this, when <i>can </i>I?

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.660
You are suspicious of me.

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:56.290
In this state, I will be unable 
to exert my full strength.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:59.500
In a worst-case scenario, 
there will be damage

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.220
to your personality after we separate.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.420
Cut the crap!

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:06.680
Don't try to gloss things over with 
a bunch of "trust" garbage, not now.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.430
We'll talk about this later.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.400
Very well.

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:13.360
Let's go.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.150
Now <i>this </i>is unexpected.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.320
They're in contact with the 
Providence Breaker and her group.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.410
Well, well, if it isn't a Dragoon...

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.040
Manifest class two divine retribution 
enforcement configuration.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.710
Avoid confrontations as much as 
possible and get into the ship!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:34.720
Hurry!

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.590
The proxies are coming ashore 
off our starboard flank!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:46.010
What?

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.650
Don't look! Shut off the monitors!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.120
My master.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.740
As I suspected, our 
synchronization is incomplete.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.820
As long as you mistrust me,

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.580
I will be unable to provide 
you with sufficient...

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.580
Shut up, damn it!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.560
So, this is the influence of the Peacemakers?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.020
The power of Providence?

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:39.320
What is this Providence 
you keep talking about?

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:44.070
Something like a set of rules that humanity 
is utterly incapable of disobeying.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.120
"Humans must obey Peacemakers."

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.740
It's a rule that's set in stone.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.830
Set in stone? Where?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.140
It's been etched into our minds 
since the day we were born.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.710
Since we were born?

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.670
You mean everyone all over the world?

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.460
There is only one exception.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.220
Commonly known as the Scrapped Princess.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.760
In other words, only you.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:09.890
That's the reason that the Peacemakers 
are trying to eliminate you.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.010
You're kidding.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.270
Just because I don't do 
what they tell me to do?

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:17.190
But even if I myself can disobey 
those monsters, it doesn't...

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.650
Your ability to cancel out 
Providence is contagious.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.070
Although it's incomplete 
right now, and only manifests

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:29.320
when your life is in danger or when 
you're under emotional stress.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.160
Contagious? You mean I'm a disease?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:36.920
Plus, the Peacemakers can't attack 
the breaker of divine law directly.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:41.310
The Peacemakers haven't attacked 
you directly so far, right?

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.130
Yeah, that's right...

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.610
By rallying around you,

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.890
mankind can form its first 
military force to defy the gods.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.180
This is a revolution!

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.820
If we're going to fight those monsters,

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:56.850
we have to have your help!

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.900
H-Hey, wait a minute!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:02.900
You can talk about revolution all you 
want, but I... What am I supposed to do?

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.320
You're our only hope.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:10.410
The last thing I want is to have 
to rely on a spoiled little girl.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.790
But this is what happens 
after just one look at them.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:18.250
We'll be slaughtered without 
even being able to fight back!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.680
Like I said, what am I 
supposed to do about it?

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.750
Even if I wanted to help you, 
there's nothing I can...

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.840
If I chop off an ear or something, will 
<i>that</i> put you under some emotional stress?!

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:30.930
Princess Senes!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.310
Don't hide behind your 
brother and sister forever!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.520
This is something that only you can do!

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:41.440
So at least <i>try </i>to do something 
on your own, Pacifica Cassul.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.670
Have faith in me, my master.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:03.710
If this keeps up, we will...

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.340
Trust doesn't come that easy!

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:27.230
It fled into phase space, huh? No matter.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.280
Let's clean house while it's away, shall we?

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.910
Lehenhof squad, two men down!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.370
Barks squad, retreating to block 3!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.960
All personnel, fall back 
to the central block!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.920
Seal all corridor bulkheads as you go!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.800
Don't wait for stragglers!

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.550
Just a minute... Why 
won't you wait for them?!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.930
If we seal those bulkheads too late,

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.350
the people who made it in 
time will be killed, too.

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:55.970
But still...!

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:57.970
We're no match for them!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:00.920
All we can do is turn tail and run, right?!

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.940
It's no use!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.110
I... I can't stand this. Please, help them!

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:12.820
Pacifica?

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.820
Don't let any of them die!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.330
I don't want anyone else to die!

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:24.750
I don't need you to tell me...

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.990
Princess Senes!

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:34.540
Oh, now I get it. That's 
what that was just now?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.850
I was expecting something more, I don't know,

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.350
like a bright flash or something.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.350
Anyway, it seems to be contagious, all right.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.730
The proxy?! Damn!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.900
Humans, hear me and obey.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.110
Bound beast, be thou released!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.110
Destroy her. Destroy the Scrapped Princess,

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.610
For you are the rod of destruction!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.610
The poison of the world.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.210
Finish it off!

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:08.500
Princess, now that we've been 
immunized by Pacifica's power,

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.210
I think that this is our chance.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:11.710
What?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:15.050
Put together as many teams of 
wizards and soldiers as possible.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.140
If they lure them in one at 
a time inside the bulkheads

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.000
and attack them with annihilation spells 
and physical attacks to their cores,

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.390
I believe they can defeat 
around half of them.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.640
I see where you're going.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.100
But what do we do about the other half?

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.660
Those are for you and me.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.110
I like your style.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:31.570
Big sis...

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.690
My proxies are being destroyed?

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:39.030
Her ability to break divine 
law has manifested, I see.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.700
In that case, I'll have to see to it myself.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.610
How foolish.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:49.960
Do you seriously think you can 
defeat me without a Dragoon?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.420
Now, Zefiris!

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.840
Manifest class two divine...

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.270
Cin?

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:12.730
It's Cz.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:15.270
Walk away, Dragoon.

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:16.490
What?

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.630
I'm not interested in 
having us kill each other.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.450
Once I've retrieved Steyr, I will withdraw.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.990
Withdrawing would be a wise move, my master.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:29.420
An Artillery-type like Cz would put a 
great strain on us in our current state.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.250
Come to the capital of Leinwan.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.000
What?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:35.420
We can no longer exterminate you in secrecy.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.640
And so we will name the place 
where this will be settled.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.220
You have a grace period of fifteen days.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:43.590
For every day you are late, 
I will kill 1,000 people.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.980
As this world's caretakers, 
we must terminate both you

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.330
and your younger sister 
by any means necessary.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:55.400
We have concluded that even destroying a 
country is acceptable to achieve that end.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:57.610
It is, is it?

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.200
We will be waiting.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.000
What the...?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:09.960
Shannon...

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.610
The proxies have disappeared!

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.420
We're saved!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.040
I'm not detecting any anywhere!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.220
Let's get verification.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:18.110
Looks like we're saved...

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.540
We are gathered here to send off the 
brave spirits of our fallen heroes!

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.310
A moment of silence!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.440
Um...

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.990
This was all because of me, wasn't it?

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.620
Don't be so full of yourself.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:47.990
They died fighting to reclaim our world.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.580
They didn't do it for you.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.410
What're you going to do now?

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.990
I'm going to put an end to this.

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.770
I'm not that princess there,

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.880
but I'm not going to lose anyone else.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.230
The sea sure is pretty, huh?

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:07.850
What is it about this world that's wrong?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.600
I'm sorry, Shannon. Raquel.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.790
What's the point of you apologizing?

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:15.200
It's like...

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.070
after hearing all that stuff, I 
understand things less and less now.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.200
What exactly <i>am </i>I?

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.990
What am I supposed to do?

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.910
We're only human, nothing more.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.030
All we can do is try the best we can.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.750
Let's go home. Back to Leinwan.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.440
The three siblings make for the 
capital in the mobile fortress.

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:39.170
The storm of an undreamt-of foreign culture

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:41.130
lashes at Pacifica and the others one by one.

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:43.250
Will they be able to 
accomplish their objectives

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:45.560
without being tossed about 
by cultural revolution?

00:22:45.560 --> 00:22:47.420
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:48.920
"Distant Ricordanza."

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
